# Copy to mobile/.env for local development.
#
# Without this the app cannot reach the backend at all: the API modules read
# `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL ?? ''`, so an unset value makes every
# request a relative path — which resolves to nothing on a device.
#
# The deployed API is the simplest thing that works everywhere, including on a
# physical handset over mobile data:
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://team21-ca.livelycoast-bbf4360d.southafricanorth.azurecontainerapps.io
#
# To point at an API running on your own machine instead, note that a phone
# cannot reach "localhost" — that address is the phone:
#
#   Android emulator   http://10.0.2.2:8000    (the emulator's alias for the host)
#   iOS simulator      http://127.0.0.1:8000   (shares the host's loopback)
#   Physical device    http://<your-LAN-IP>:8000
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables at bundle time, so changing this needs a
# full reload rather than a refresh, and only *static* dot-notation references
# are substituted. That last point matters: src/config/env.ts reads
# `process.env[expoKey]` with a computed key, which Expo cannot inline — every
# value it exposes is therefore always its hardcoded fallback, whatever is set
# here. Only `logger.ts` consumes it (LOG_LEVEL), so nothing important depends
# on it today, but do not add API configuration there expecting it to work.
#
# Never put a secret behind this prefix — the value ships inside the app bundle
# in plain text.
